[h1]Transport Fever 2 Multiplayer[/h1][i]Mod version: 0.6.1.14 -- free and open source (MIT)[/i]
Play Transport Fever 2 together. This mod adds real multiplayer to the game: several players build roads, railways, stations, depots, vehicles and lines in [b]one shared world at the same time[/b]. Everything one player builds appears for everyone, at the same moment of the simulation on every machine. Play one company together, or give every player a company of their own on the same map.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]This Workshop Item Is a Signpost[/h2]The mod needs native components beside the game (a few DLLs and a small lobby program) that the Workshop cannot deliver, so [b]subscribing here installs nothing that plays[/b]. Subscribing is harmless: the item does nothing when enabled, and a save that lists it loads everywhere. The mod itself comes from the website:
[url=https://silver2127.github.io/tpf2-multiplayer/]silver2127.github.io/tpf2-multiplayer[/url]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Early Access Notice[/h2]The game has no network code of its own; this mod adds lockstep multiplayer from outside, reverse-engineered without the engine's source. It is [b]experimental[/b]. Expect the occasional desync, a build that does not replicate, or a crash, especially in long sessions on big maps. Keep your own saves. Sessions of up to four players have been run, on one PC and between PCs on different networks. Bug reports with logs are very welcome and are what moves the mod forward.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Installation[/h2][b]Windows (Steam version of the game)[/b]
[olist][*] Download [b]TpF2Multiplayer.msi[/b] from the [url=https://github.com/silver2127/tpf2-multiplayer/releases/latest]latest release[/url]
[*] Close the game and run the installer; it finds the game folder through Steam
[*] Start the game: the title menu has a new [b]MULTIPLAYER[/b] button[/olist][b]Linux and Steam Deck (the Windows game under Proton)[/b]
[olist][*] In Steam, set the game to run with Proton 9 or newer, start it once and quit
[*] Download [b]install_proton.sh[/b] from the same release page and run [b]sh install_proton.sh[/b]; it installs the same files into the Proton game[/olist]Every player in a session needs the [b]same mod version[/b]. A new version is installed the same way, over the old one; there is no in-game updater. To uninstall, remove it from Windows Apps or run the installer again and choose Remove; the game's own files are put back.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]How to Play[/h2][olist][*] Title menu, [b]MULTIPLAYER[/b], [b]HOST GAME[/b]. The join code is copied to your clipboard; send it to your friends, or tick [b]PUBLIC[/b] to list the game for anyone. A password locks the code.
[*] Friends open [b]MULTIPLAYER[/b], paste the code and press [b]JOIN GAME[/b], or click your game under [b]PUBLIC GAMES[/b].
[*] The host presses [b]START GAME[/b]. The host's newest save goes to everyone automatically, mods included; then everyone opens [b]LOAD GAME[/b] and picks [b]mp_shared[/b].
[*] Build. Every road, station, vehicle and line appears for all players.[/olist]A new game has the multiplayer mod enabled by itself; for an existing save, enable it once in the save's Mods panel. The host's PC should have UDP port 29471 reachable (the lobby tries UPnP first). If that is not possible, play on the [b]public dedicated test server[/b] in the PUBLIC GAMES list, where nobody needs an open port. It runs all day.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Features[/h2][list][*] [b]One shared world[/b]: every build, purchase, sale, line edit and demolition is applied at the same simulation step on every machine, the builder's own included
[*] [b]Shared company or one company per player[/b], each with its own money, and station permissions between companies
[*] [b]Hot join[/b]: a player can join a running game; the session holds while they load, then carries on
[*] [b]Automatic save and mod transfer[/b]: the host's save and the mods it needs go to every joiner, over a fast direct channel
[*] [b]Works through home routers[/b]: hole punching first, a relay through the project's server when the punch cannot work
[*] [b]Public game list and join codes[/b], with an optional password
[*] [b]Session speed voting[/b]: the players agree on the game speed; the world pauses for everyone or for no one
[*] [b]Desync detection[/b]: the worlds are compared continuously, and a resync from the host's save is one click
[*] [b]Dedicated server[/b]: a headless host that keeps a world up for anyone to join
[*] [b]Nothing phones home[/b]: no telemetry, no statistics, no crash upload. The only network use is the public game list, the join rendezvous and your session ([url=https://silver2127.github.io/tpf2-multiplayer/privacy.html]privacy policy[/url])[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Requirements[/h2][list][*] Transport Fever 2 on Steam, build 35924 (Windows, or Linux / Steam Deck through Proton)
[*] The same mod version on every player's PC
[*] For a host: UDP port 29471 reachable, or use the dedicated server
[*] The mods a session uses are sent to joiners automatically; Workshop mods are registered on the joiner's side without a second download[/list]Big maps are welcome: the mod installs alongside [url=https://github.com/silver2127/tpf2-bigmap]TpF2 Big Maps[/url], in either order.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Troubleshooting[/h2]Most problems are fixed by a [b]rejoin[/b] or a [b]resync[/b] (the RESYNC button in the Multiplayer window reloads the host's save on every machine). Before reporting a bug, please try these:
[list][*] Make sure every player runs the same mod version; the lobby refuses a different one
[*] Have the affected player leave the session and join again
[*] If the world drifted (a DESYNC line in the window), press RESYNC on the host
[*] If nobody can connect to you, check the host's port or use the dedicated server
[*] Steam's "Verify integrity of game files" removes the mod's hook; run the installer's Repair to bring the MULTIPLAYER button back[/list][b]Known Issues[/b]
[list][*] [b]A player more than 15 units behind the others[/b] has their actions held until they catch up; wait, or lower the session speed
[*] [b]A second game on the same PC[/b] does not get the hooks; one instance per Windows session
[*] [b]A four-arm track crossing built as one piece[/b] freezes the game; build it as two straight lines
[*] [b]Some stop and line details do not replicate yet[/b] (a stop's load settings, replacing a stop on an occupied platform); the full list is in KNOWN_ISSUES.md on GitHub[/list]If a problem persists, open an issue on GitHub with a short description and the logs from [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\tpf2mp\logs[/b] (Proton: the same path inside the game's prefix). Logs from everyone involved speed things up enormously.
[url=https://github.com/silver2127/tpf2-multiplayer/issues]Issue tracker[/url]
[hr][/hr]
